{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510044-mass-paralyze","id":1510044,"title":"Mass Paralyze","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-29T00:01:40-07:00","id":1510044,"title":"Mass Paralyze","content":"So, a friend and I were discussing a character's concept he wants to create, and among other things we were discussing, he said he wanted to be able to try an effect similar to mass paralyze that we often see in D&amp;D games (he came from D&amp;D lol) and I said that from what I remember it would require Forces 4. Do you agree with that, are the other more efficient ways to implement this effect that I'm not remembering (without Time as he doesn't like Time Sphere)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T04:15:26-07:00","id":1510055,"title":"","content":"If it is to stop living things only, then it could be possible with Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T10:41:08-07:00","id":1510111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510044-mass-paralyze?p=1510055#post1510055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is to stop living things only, then it could be possible with Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life seems like another option, it's strange because I found literally no mention of such feat in &quot;How do you DO that?&quot;. It's a staple kind of magic found in many stories about magic, I thought it was weird that there isn't a single mention of it in a book dedicated to this sort of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T06:35:00-07:00","id":1510194,"title":"","content":"Forces will certainly stop them in their tracks. And you've said locking them in Time is not an option. Instead, they might use a Life Effect to paralyze the target's muscles. Mind can also be used to immobilize a target by arresting their cognitive functions, though not strictly <i>paralyzing</i>. Finally, Correspondence should be able to lock them in space in the same way that Time can lock someone in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","name":"Hasnamuss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27764_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T09:10:37-07:00","id":1510205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hasnamuss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510044-mass-paralyze?p=1510194#post1510194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces will certainly stop them in their tracks. And you've said locking them in Time is not an option. Instead, they might use a Life Effect to paralyze the target's muscles. Mind can also be used to immobilize a target by arresting their cognitive functions, though not strictly <i>paralyzing</i>. Finally, Correspondence should be able to lock them in space in the same way that Time can lock someone in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, he doesn't want to use Time and he was also worried after reading you can't use Sphere Magick with Time, so that he wants to freeze people in place to later attempt other magical attacks and as he also loves Forces (not strange for someone coming from D&amp;D lol) I suggested Forces, but these other possibilities are also very interesting, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T10:34:25-07:00","id":1510210,"title":"","content":"It depends on the concept you want to apply, if you use gravity or something related I would say Force 4, if it is paralyzing through some mental effect Mind 4 or 5, if it is something biological Life 4, at least, Time would obviously also work, now to to affect multiple targets you would need to combine with Correspondence 3 unleast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T17:57:41-07:00","id":1510298,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think that would be necessary if you were in the presence of all the multiple targets; you'd just need extra successes to affect more than one. I think a mage could also achieve much the same result with crafty use of mental illusions at Mind 3 (make them think they're bound in tight chains, trapped in a thorny thicket, surrounded by poisonous snakes on every side, etc.).<br /> <br /> You could also prevent someone from moving or doing anything <i>effectively</i> with Entropy 3 and enough successes to Final Destination them into giving up the attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T18:45:51-07:00","id":1510301,"title":"","content":"As far as I learned the rule of thumb to use on multiple targets already requires some use of correspondence, perhaps except entropy, a somewhat debatable thing in mage is that the system of spheres gives freedom to do a lot, but also generates disagreements about which sphere to use for every situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:07:56-07:00","id":1510361,"title":"","content":"Life, Forces, Time, and Mind could all work. <br /> <br /> If its Forces I it is Forces 3 to immobilize everything in a small area or in several small areas (those just around the targets). <br /> <br /> Life 3 would be the spell to biologically paralyze them, I think. You aren't changing their pattern just blocking something from happening.<br /> <br /> It takes level 4 in Mind to control someone. Though you could use an illusion to trick them into not wanting to move, actual immobilization needs Mind 4.<br /> <br /> Time 3 can slow people to the point that they are functionally not moving, though they're not going to notice because their senses are slowed too. Contrary to what your friend says, a Mage using this effect on someone else does not lose the ability to cast other spells. The rule he is thinking of is actually about limitations on extra actions. To keep people from breaking the game a Mage who gives himself extra actions can only use one of them for spellcasting. <br /> <br /> With Correspondence I can think of two effects that would functionally immobilize someone. The first is to stretch the space around someone so they can make no significant progress towards moving. That sounds like a Corr 5. The second is to use Wards on the areas around your targets such that they prevent the person from leaving. That would be Corr 4. <br /> <br /> None of these <i>need</i> to be locked as far as I can see. The Forces, Time ones can be if you want to by adding Life 2. The main advantage is that the spell continues even if the target is moved. That's true of the Correspondence spell as well, though since it wards against any form of moving out of the zone it is largely pointless to lock it*.<br /> <br /> The Life spell doesn't need any extra Spheres to be treated as locked and I'd leave it up to the player to decide. I'd treat the Mind spell the same way.<br /> <br /> *If you modified the spell, though, so that it prevented anyone but the target from moving him out of his exact location and you locked that one to him, you would replicate the classic Freedom of Movement effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T03:00:25-07:00","id":1510767,"title":"","content":"I think we're underestimating the utility of Matter in restricting someone's movement.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 (for shifting between solid to liquid) to make the ground beneath their feet into mud, that they then sink into. Either allow the Effect to wear off immediately after, or just let them wallow in thick muck. (You might even do this coincidentally, if you &quot;reveal&quot; the ground they just stepped on was &quot;really quicksand&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Matter 2 can turn a person's clothes into a solid, rigid substance. Like stone or metal. They can't run around or attack if their shirt and pants are now made of tungston.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 can reshape the ground into a perfectly frictionless surface (or smooth enough). For that matter (haha), you could toss an unidentified liquid onto the ground, then convert it with Matter 2 into some kind of oil or grease. Either way, the person will spend all their effort just remaining upright (if they even can), much less attacking you. (A similar Effect can be achieved with Forces 2, by disrupting the force of friction itself).<br /> <br /> You can always use Matter 3 to change and reshape materials in the environment into a snare, wrapping around the person's body to trap them.<br /> <br /> <br /> As is probably obvious, these are less &quot;paralysis&quot; in the traditional sense, and more various forms of trapping or disabling. But really, it's a distinction without a difference. If all you want is someone stopped, it matters little exactly how. Matter is very good at turning the environment against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}